<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs rise in week.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe rose by three to 59 rigs in the week to Sept 4, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>The gains were all in Norway where activity rose three to 14 rigs, Andersen said.</p>
<p>Rigs active in the U.K. held steady at 30 while there were five rigs active in Denmark, also flat on the week. Dutch and Irish activity was unchanged at nine rigs and one rig respectively.</p>
<p>Onshore drilling activity was unchanged at three rigs, two in the U.K. and one on the Faroe Islands.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
